Fuzzy-search the whole workspace from the composer's "@" menu.

Upstream's "@" menu browses one folder at a time: "@auth" only finds auth.ts
at the workspace root, and reaching a nested file means opening each folder.
Once the workspace's file index (server patch 0011-mention-file-index.patch)
has loaded, typing a name now matches every file and folder fzf-style, like
Claude Code's and Codex's own pickers: the characters must appear in order
but not together, so "@srvts" finds src/server.ts. Matches in the file name,
at word and camel-case boundaries, and in a row rank higher, files a little
above folders, shorter paths above longer ones. "@src/au" searches all of
src. A bare "@" and "@<folder>/" still browse, so Enter on a folder result
opens it and Tab attaches it whole. Rows show the matched characters in bold
and the folder each result is in. Once 50 results are in hand, a path whose
best possible score can't beat the 50th is skipped before it's matched,
which keeps a keystroke near a millisecond on a kernel-sized workspace.
Without the index (still loading, or an older runner) the menu filters the
folder as before. The new-session launcher's "@" menu, which reads the
host's filesystem, is unchanged.
Base: omnigent v0.18.0 (a8676d23e88d), after 0001-0013.

